      {
        "id": "p83-q4-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find the initial population and the limiting population.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Initial population: 20 yabbies. Limiting population: 300 yabbies.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y(0)&=\\frac{300}{1+14}\\\\&=20.\\end{align*}$$\nAs $t\\to\\infty$, $e^{-0.4t}\\to0$, so $y\\to300$.\nThe population starts at 20 yabbies and approaches a limit of 300 yabbies.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 19
      },
      {
        "id": "p83-q4-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find the population when it is growing fastest.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "150 yabbies.",
          "worked": "For a logistic model, the growth rate is greatest at half the limiting population.\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=\\frac{300}{2}\\\\&=150.\\end{align*}$$\nThe population is growing fastest at 150 yabbies.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 15
      },
      {
        "id": "p83-q4-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Find the exact time at which it is growing fastest.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{5}{2}\\ln14$ months after release.",
          "worked": "Set $y=150$:\n$$\\begin{align*}150&=\\frac{300}{1+14e^{-0.4t}}\\\\1+14e^{-0.4t}&=2\\\\e^{-0.4t}&=\\frac{1}{14}\\\\-0.4t&=\\ln\\frac{1}{14}\\\\t&=\\frac{5}{2}\\ln14\\text{ months}.\\end{align*}$$\nThis is approximately $6.6$ months after release.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 37
      }
    ]
